"]}, "overview": "Texas's 15th District pairs first-term Republican incumbent Monica De La Cruz against Democrat and Tejano music star Bobby Pulido in one of the most watched House races of 2026. The district leans Republican by about 7 points, and De La Cruz holds a clear cash advantage, but Pulido has raised nearly $3 million and drawn seven-figure outside support from Democrats focused on winning back South Texas Hispanic voters.\n\nThe two most recent polls, including a nonpartisan August survey, show Pulido ahead by about five points, and prediction markets price his win odds near 80 percent. Expert raters remain split between tossup and Republican lean, reflecting genuine uncertainty in a low-turnout midterm environment. The race sits as a narrow Democratic lean with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}]}